# Project structure

Standard Go module layout:

| Path | Holds |
|------|--------|
| `cmd/tabui/` | Binary entry (`main`) — wire only |
| `internal/<feature>/` | Private app packages (providers, matching, types) |
| `internal/ui/` | TUI only (Bubble Tea views, styles, list rendering) |
| `internal/<name>/` | Shared helper package only when used by **2+** callers (e.g. `internal/fuzzy`) — never a dump `utils` package |

## Colocation

Related code that is **not** reused across the project stays in the **same feature package**. Do not invent global `types/` or `utils/` buckets.

```text
# ✅ GOOD — feature-local types and helpers
internal/package_scripts/
  provider.go
  types.go      # only used here
  parse.go      # only used here

# ❌ BAD — splitting one feature across global buckets
internal/types/package_scripts.go
internal/utils/parse_package_json.go   # only package_scripts needs it
```

## Shared helpers

Promote to a **named** package under `internal/` (e.g. `internal/fuzzy`) only when a **second** caller needs it.

## Boundaries

- `internal/ui` must not contain provider matching or filesystem / manifest business logic.
- Feature packages under `internal/` must not render the TUI; they return suggestions (`label`, `detail`, `value`).
